WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.710
<i>The scripture picture books Main had 
created were now on the market.</i>

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.290
<i>However...</i>

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.720
There's no doubt about it...

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.680
It's ink.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.650
If we're going to prioritize safety,

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.450
we might want to have Main start 
staying at the cathedral now.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.190
What?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.490
I don't want to be away from all of you,

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.100
but I'd regret it even more if something 
were to happen to any of you,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.590
so I'll go to the cathedral.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.490
<i>Main tried to put on 
a brave face, but...</i>

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.520
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.030
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.980
<b>Chapter 28
The Story About Winter Stays and the Future</b>

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.250
It's morning already?

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.840
Lady Main!

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.300
Please stay in bed until you're summoned.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:32.080
Oh, really? Sorry.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.550
And don't apologize to your attendants.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:39.540
<i>Even though we didn't have books at 
home, I was able to talk to Tuuli.</i>

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:47.730
That is all for today.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.430
Then I shall go help the head priest.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:56.090
Lady Main, after speaking 
with the head priest,

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.740
he has instructed me to tell you

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.750
that you may not leave your room 
until we have more information.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.780
Huh?! But that means... 
I can't even go to the library?

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.950
I thought I'd somehow make it 
through if I had my books!

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:11.300
Talk about gloom and doom.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:16.080
Lady Main, let's think about who should 
be your chef during your stay here.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.290
We'll need to find an assistant 
from the orphanage for Ella.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.390
Right. I wonder who'd be a good candidate.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.670
Please take your time thinking about it.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.000
There's still plenty of time.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:31.400
Lady Main, if you have time,
 please show me how to do arithmetic.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.540
Sure, of course.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.320
See? If you do this, it's easy.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.510
Yes. You're a surprisingly 
good teacher, Lady Main.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.550
Far better than Gil.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.630
Well, I was teaching 
people at the gate,

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:52.090
so maybe I could be a teacher 
for the cathedral classroom.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:56.710
Lady Main, what do you mean by 
this "cathedral classroom"?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.500
A place where people can learn 
how to read and write.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.220
The more people who learn how 
to read letters and books,

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:09.420
there'll be people who can write and 
then we'll get even more books!

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.050
Then we'll get lots, and lots, and lots...

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:16.910
Many, many more books to read!

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:21.250
Yay!

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.000
Thank you!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:30.400
Lady Main, I'm afraid I haven't 
been informed of such a place...

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.990
I mean, we have karuta and picture books,

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:35.200
so I'm pretty sure most of 
us can read a little now.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.250
But I want you to be able to write, too.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.120
That'll make your job as an attendant

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.040
or when you come work at the workshop 
or orphanage much easier.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:47.660
Would I be able to 
write reports by myself?!

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.380
Then I wanna learn!

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:51.900
I'll make sure to teach you 
everything you need to know.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:55.940
Lady Main, a grey-robed priest 
should be the one teaching.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.230
You mustn't bother with 
such a thing, Lady Main.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.060
Okay...

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.390
Main, you okay?

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.750
Lutz!

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.390
Whoa.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.110
Hug me.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.080
I wanna go home.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.130
It's only been a day.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.510
I'm so lonely without my family.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.080
I might actually die from loneliness.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.010
That's seriously not funny coming from you.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.830
Honestly, if you're going to hug 
someone, it should be a rich noble.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.580
Lady Main relies way too much on Lutz.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.980
<i>Then we talked about the 
hand work for the winter.</i>

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.670
<i>We can't make paper in the winter,</i>

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:45.490
<i>so we decided to make a Reversi set, 
a chess set, and playing cards out of wood.</i>

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.380
All right. First, let's make a pattern.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:55.600
I wouldn't lose to Lutz if 
I had a writing tablet, too!

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.990
I'll prepare one for you 
once spring comes along,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.770
since you know how to write 
and do arithmetic now.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.560
Really? Yay!

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:04.970
Then I'll be on the same 
level as Lutz and Fran!

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.520
The same?

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.360
Yeah! Because if I get a writing tablet,

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.730
that'll mean I've been acknowledged 
just like Lutz and Fran!

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.860
That settles it! I'm 
definitely beating Lutz!

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:18.510
Yeah, hurry up and beat me already.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.340
Otherwise, it'll be an issue for me, too.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.060
And why is that?

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:27.250
I'm going to tour a papyrus workshop
 in a neighboring city this spring.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.730
A neighboring city?

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:31.990
What do you want to do in life, Lutz?

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:32.900
Me?

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.330
I want to travel to other cities.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:38.820
Other cities?

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.330
I wanna become a traveling trader 
and see the world for myself.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.340
So your dream is coming true.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.080
Yeah.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.330
Okay, Main. I'll see you later.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:53.080
Yeah.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.110
Are you lonely, Lady Main?

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:02.320
Well, I always had my family around me.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.850
I'll coddle you like Lutz does!

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.200
Absolutely not.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.640
Gil, Lady Main is your master.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:18.650
It is not your duty as her 
attendant to coddle her.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:21.340
You and Lutz are not the same.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.290
Fine...

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:29.420
Lady Main, I can imagine you're lonely 
due to the current circumstances.

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:36.710
When your family or Lutz are here to see 
you, I can overlook them spoiling you.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:42.550
However,  I would like you to keep an
 appropriate distance with your attendants.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.240
Okay.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:52.580
Main, it's like you're a little baby again.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:57.910
Well, I'm lonely, and 
Mom can't come, either.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.150
But I'm not lonely when we're like this.

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:04.260
Then I'll tell you stories, 
since Mom can't come.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:06.600
Okay!

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:11.990
Once upon a time, there were 
little star children.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.440
Okay, I'll see you later, Main.

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:16.740
Come back soon, okay, Tuuli?

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:23.780
Wait...

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:28.960
Tuuli...

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:43.800
Lady Main.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:44.550
Fran.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.640
I have a message from the head priest.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.540
He would like you to have your robes

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:53.310
for the ceremony delivered when 
Master Karstedt is here.

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:56.540
Oh... all right.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:09:00.310
I'll have Lutz tell Mister Benno.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:01.620
Thank you.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:35.330
Your cooking is so delicious, Main.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:38.250
You've got some on your mouth, Main.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:41.210
Main, make sure you eat plenty, 
so you can grow big.

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:41.940
Main.

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:42.710
Main.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:43.720
Main.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:44.890
Main.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:45.980
Main.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.190
Main.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.370
Main.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:49.270
Main.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.500
Main.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:10.510
<i>The colder it got, the 
more homesick I became.</i>

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.920
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:21.010
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:24.260
<i>On the day of the first 
snowfall of the year...</i>

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:28.350
Mister Benno! I missed you!

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:32.780
How depressing.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:36.240
What's wrong? You look rather pale.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:41.170
I'm going to be speaking with the 
head priest and an upper-class noble.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.600
I'm getting a headache 
just thinking about it.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:46.250
Sir, you're going to mess up your hair.

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:49.110
Wait, are you actually nervous?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:54.050
You're always more than happy to start 
fights with the guild master and vested interests.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.250
Don't group the guild master 
and upper-class nobles together!

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:01.300
Oh, don't even worry. 
Lord Karstedt is a good person.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.980
You simpleton!

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:07.270
There's no way I'd be summoned to the 
cathedral just to deliver your robes!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.000
Huh?

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.590
They're clearly trying to gather 
more information about you.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.600
Without a doubt.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.060
Thank you all for gathering here today.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:20.790
First, let's have a look 
at her ceremonial robes.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:24.570
These are Lady Main's ceremonial robes.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.170
Well done, Benno.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.120
Next, I would like for 
Apprentice Priestess Main...

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.000
to accept these robes.

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:39.620
I humbly accept.

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:52.670
Stop this, Schicicoza!

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:53.700
Quiet, Damuel.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.940
Know your place.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.940
Damuel. Tell the truth.

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:02.000
When Schicicoza told me to know my place,

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:06.300
I couldn't stop him anymore.

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:09.990
I'm terribly sorry!

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.450
Why...

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:19.450
Karstedt, Damuel. Your punishment 
has come to an end for now.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:27.740
<i>From there, due to Mister Benno's 
request to know the opinions of nobles,</i>

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:30.720
<i>I had the head priest take 
a look at my handiwork.</i>

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:34.720
If you're going to sell these in the 
lower parts of the city, I see no issue.

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.720
<i>The magical item that prevents eavesdropping.</i>

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:44.370
Enschupot.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.760
<i>What is this?</i>

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.710
<i>I see.</i>

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:02.140
<i>He set up this boundary for Mister 
Benno, since he doesn't have any mana.</i>

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:05.630
Now then, Benno... I have 
something I'd like to ask you.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:07.130
Please, go right ahead.

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:11.150
Is the head of the Ink 
Guild without a doubt Wolf?

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:14.160
Yes.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:18.070
Ever since you established 
a magical contract with them,

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:23.970
they started investigating Main, 
and Lutz became their prime target.

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:25.660
Is this also true?

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:27.530
It is.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:32.160
Usually, I'll gather as much 
information as possible

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.830
before establishing a contract, 
to put us at a slight advantage.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:39.680
I cannot fathom why he'd want information 
after the contract has been signed.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:42.660
Are you acquainted with this man, Main?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.950
No. I have not seen his face, 
nor do I know his name.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:50.680
Mister Benno had me hide while 
they established the contract.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:53.560
A wise decision, Benno.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:14:01.300
Perhaps the reason Wolf openly gathered 
information after forming the contract

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:07.080
was because he didn't care if things went 
south after the contract was in place.

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.470
May I ask what you mean?

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:13.930
Contract magic cannot be undone unless 
everyone in the contract agrees to it.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:16.110
I'm assuming he was trying 
to take advantage of that.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:20.320
I had only heard bad rumors about him, but...

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:22.110
What kind of rumors?

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:27.340
In order to gain the favor of nobles, 
he's willing to commit crimes.

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:29.210
Crimes?!

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:31.940
I'm not entirely sure 
just how true this is...

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:36.100
What do you think Wolf intended to do 
after getting information on Main?

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:39.850
Lady Main's greatest asset is her ability 
to create one product after another,

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.600
and her knowledge of how 
to create these items.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:49.600
He could either kidnap Lady 
Main to gain this knowledge...

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:53.990
Or take those closest to her hostage and 
demand this knowledge be handed over.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:56.740
Knowledge?

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:59.750
<i>Yeah, I'm sure this all sounds unbelievable.</i>

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:05.270
However, imprisoning Lady Main is far more 
difficult than kidnapping her in her case.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:06.620
True.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.780
She'll run a fever for a few days

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.210
after putting her in the 
reflection room for half a day.

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:14.270
She'll die before they can get 
any information out of her.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.270
Meaning it's probably likely 
that he'd sell her off

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.780
to some noble after gaining 
some of her knowledge.

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:25.020
Sell me off?!

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:30.270
Or he could try to force a subordination 
contract through her Devouring.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.790
Seems likely.

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:38.010
Benno, I'd like you to continue gathering 
information through your workplace,

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:40.660
and continue to conceal 
Main's existence here.

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:42.980
As you wish.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:51.310
<i>Then we had Damuel join in, so they could 
discuss the judgment their superior</i>

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:54.580
<i>had given them for incompetence during 
their mission to subjugate the trombe.</i>

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:59.420
The judgment the lord had 
passed upon Schicicoza is death.

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:03.450
As far as the public knows, 
Schicicoza died in the line of duty.

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:05.390
<i>As far as the public knows?</i>

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:10.420
Karstedt and Damuel have paid for your robes.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:13.270
Oh, so that's why he paid 
Mister Benno earlier.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:17.070
Damuel has been demoted to apprentice status.

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:19.920
He will be your bodyguard for the next year.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:20.840
Huh?

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:26.660
You are truly in danger.

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:28.720
Word has spread among the upper-class nobles

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:32.880
that there's an apprentice 
priestess who can be exploited,

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:34.770
given the amount of mana you have.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:41.140
And that you had been granted 
blue robes by the lord.

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:42.140
<i>Do you see?</i>

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:46.340
<i>That's the apprentice priestess who was 
granted blue robes by the church and the lord.</i>

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:50.300
<i>That's the first time I've heard any of that.</i>

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:53.270
<i>You dumb noble.</i>

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:56.770
After finding out she was given 
her blue robes by the lord,

00:16:56.770 --> 00:17:00.280
I'm sure nobles who want to get close
 to her will try to curry favor with him.

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:02.920
Even if it means having you kidnapped

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:05.280
just so they can save you 
and the lord feels indebted.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.890
And if they're someone who opposes the lord,

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:12.100
they could kidnap you and sell you 
off to one of his enemies,

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:15.250
or even claim that you're their child.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.730
And in that case, your 
family would be in the way.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:21.510
They would probably be silenced.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.910
Among the lower-class nobles,

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:29.030
there is still much contempt 
towards the apprentice priestess.

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.850
I'm sure they'd rather not 
acknowledge an apprentice priestess

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:34.900
who's a commoner having so much mana.

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:39.640
Even I couldn't believe this 
to be true until I saw her.

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:50.610
And Schicicoza's mother was delighted 
that Schicicoza came home

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:52.580
due to the purge.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:55.350
I heard that she bears great resentment

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:57.700
towards the apprentice priestess 
due to what just happened.

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:00.560
Resentment towards me?

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:04.180
If she wants to go as far as sacrificing her 
own family for the sake of revenge,

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:05.450
things will get ugly.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:07.270
Main.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.020
Yes?

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:12.270
I was going to eventually have 
you marry a noble.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:13.340
Huh?

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:18.160
It is extremely likely that you and those 
around you will be thrown into danger.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.780
You should have a noble adopt 
you as soon as possible.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.780
Adopt me?

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:26.830
Yes. If you were adopted by Karstedt,

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.950
you could be protected to some degree.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.420
I assure you that he is a good man.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.680
Main, would you like to become my daughter?

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:37.090
I can't!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:41.120
And what do you mean by that, Main?

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:50.060
I want to go home.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:52.530
I don't want to be apart 
from my family any longer.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.420
Main, calm down.

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:05.050
We're going into my workshop to make 
sure the effects of this are minimal.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.290
I know the Dedication Ceremony
 is approaching,

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.180
but you've held in too much mana.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:15.540
You fool.

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:17.910
I'm sorry...

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:22.650
To think you'd be this unstable even 
with your family visiting you...

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:24.290
Did something happen?

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.060
It's all your fault, Head Priest.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.560
You just had to go digging 
through my memories.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:34.630
Thinking about the family
 I'll never get to see again...

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:38.520
I never want to be apart 
from my current family.

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:40.040
And yet...

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.370
Main, control yourself!

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:49.780
If I let some noble adopt me, 
I'll never be able to see my family!

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:51.670
Main!

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:56.750
It calms you down to a certain 
degree when I do this, does it not?

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.510
You've still got a ways to go.

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:09.610
Hup...

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.450
This will do.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:15.550
Honestly...

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:21.780
Now, listen to me. Your 
mana is far too powerful.

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:26.030
It is enough that it should be used 
for this domain and this country.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:28.800
This country?

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:32.140
Yes. Main, you need to realize this yourself.

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:37.090
When your emotions become volatile, 
you put those around you in danger.

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:39.860
Since you cannot control your powers,

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:42.800
it is very possible to put 
your beloved family in danger.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.440
I'll be fine as long as I have my family.

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:49.930
So please... Don't separate 
me from my family!

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:54.320
Ten years old.

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:58.620
The enrollment age for the 
Royal Academy is ten.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:01.020
Until then, have your family 
spoil you as much as you'd like.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:05.270
Thank you very much!

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:10.880
But from that point on, 
I will not honor your opinions.

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:14.280
If you are deemed dangerous or harmful,

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:16.420
you will be dealt with.

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:19.950
Just remember that.

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:22.990
Okay...

00:22:57.980 --> 00:23:00.980
<b>Next Chapter
The Dedication Ceremony and Spring Arrives</b>

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:03.730
Hm... The game played with 
these resembles gewinnen.

00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:11.650
Looks like I win!

00:23:11.650 --> 00:23:13.700
I have lost?!

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:15.680
One more match! I will win the next round!

00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:18.990
If you buy Reversi, I'll 
play another game with you.

00:23:19.430 --> 00:23:21.260
Four big gold coins!

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:24.640
Considering it just costs five small 
silvers, I just made eight times more!

00:23:24.890 --> 00:23:26.450
You should always take as much money

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:29.740
as you can from wherever you can 
when the opportunity shows itself!

00:23:32.740 --> 00:23:34.480
I still don't understand.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
Illustration by Namino Ryo
